WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.080
Early the next morning, Heidi awoke to the sound of Grandfather's voice.

2
00:00:16.081 --> 00:00:17.673
"Come along, Heidi!

3
00:00:17.674 --> 00:00:20.396
The sun is up," he said.

4
00:00:20.397 --> 00:00:25.300
"Put on your best dress because we are going to church!"

5
00:00:25.301 --> 00:00:32.629
Heidi was so surprised by her Grandfather's announcement that she dressed quickly with happy anticipation.

6
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:39.077
When she came down the ladder, she saw a sight she had never seen before.

7
00:00:39.078 --> 00:00:47.021
"Why, Grandfather!" she exclaimed, "I have never seen you dress so nicely!

8
00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:51.123
Look at your handsome coat and silver buttons!"

9
00:00:51.124 --> 00:00:54.271
He tried not to smile and replied,

10
00:00:54.272 --> 00:00:58.048
"I suppose Clara gave you that nice dress.

11
00:00:58.049 --> 00:01:01.042
Well, it makes you look very pretty.

12
00:01:01.043 --> 00:01:05.264
Now come along, we don't want to be late."

13
00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:10.113
They set off hand in hand down the mountain path to the valley below.

14
00:01:10.114 --> 00:01:14.401
The church bells were ringing as they walked through the town.

15
00:01:14.402 --> 00:01:25.307
Inside the church, the townspeople had already taken their seats and the singing had begun when Heidi and her Grandfather entered.

16
00:01:25.308 --> 00:01:30.110
People turned their heads, and whispers spread from pew to pew.

17
00:01:30.111 --> 00:01:34.913
"Do you see Heidi and her Grandfather?" they said.

18
00:01:34.914 --> 00:01:38.642
"It can't be! Grandfather is in church!"

19
00:01:38.643 --> 00:01:45.893
At the end of the service, Grandfather took Heidi's hand, and they walked over to the pastor's house.

20
00:01:45.894 --> 00:01:50.572
The pastor welcomed Heidi and shook hands with Grandfather happily.

21
00:01:50.573 --> 00:01:55.236
"I have come to ask for your help, pastor," said Grandfather.

22
00:01:55.237 --> 00:02:03.432
"I have made up my mind to follow your advice and find a place for us to live in Dorfli for the winter."

23
00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:08.892
"Wonderful," said the pastor. "You are always welcome among us!"

24
00:02:08.893 --> 00:02:14.345
The pastor smiled warmly, and they talked about the different houses that were for rent.

25
00:02:14.346 --> 00:02:20.371
Grandfather thanked him for his advice, and they all walked outside to say good-bye.

26
00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:26.438
The townspeople, who had followed Grandfather to the pastor's house, were gathered outside,

27
00:02:26.439 --> 00:02:30.847
and the pastor wanted them to see that Grandfather was always welcome.

28
00:02:30.848 --> 00:02:37.041
"I look forward to spending many pleasant winter evenings together," said the pastor.

29
00:02:37.042 --> 00:02:42.138
Immediately, the people of Dorfli came up to say hello and shake Grandfather's hand.

30
00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:47.503
"We are so pleased to see you both among us!" some said.

31
00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:52.869
Others exclaimed, "I have been wishing that we could talk together again."

32
00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:58.236
Everywhere he turned, Grandfather was surprised by a friendly welcome.

33
00:02:58.237 --> 00:03:01.929
He had always thought that the people of Dorfli disliked him.

34
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:11.194
What he didn't know was that Heidi had told the baker, who brought her from the train station, how much she missed Grandfather.

35
00:03:11.195 --> 00:03:15.957
He had told the whole town what a kind man he was to Heidi.

36
00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:24.028
Grandfather explained that he was going to rent a house for the winter in Dorfli, and everyone was very happy to hear it.

37
00:03:24.029 --> 00:03:31.525
On the way home, many new and old friends walked part way up the mountain with Grandfather and Heidi.

38
00:03:31.526 --> 00:03:38.738
When they were climbing the path alone again, Heidi noticed the sunlight shining on Grandfather's face.

39
00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:44.812
"Grandfather, I have never seen you look so happy before," she said.

40
00:03:44.813 --> 00:03:51.102
"Do you think so?" asked Grandfather with a smile, "Well, yes, Heidi.

41
00:03:51.103 --> 00:03:55.240
I am happier today than I thought was possible.

42
00:03:55.241 --> 00:03:59.338
I have been angry with the people of Dorfli for too long.

43
00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:03.022
It is good to be at peace with God and friends again."

44
00:04:03.023 --> 00:04:05.916
He put his arm around Heidi's shoulders.

45
00:04:05.917 --> 00:04:13.827
"God was good to me when he sent you to my hut." Grandfather said.
